  "summary": "The netlist reproduces the intended r2 architecture exactly: 24 V input through FB8/F2 (7 A) with the 28 V TVS (D5) and a P-channel AON6407 (T6) high-side reverse-polarity stage, TPS62933 buck (U3) with correct BST/RT/SS/FB networks (C45, R24, C39, R19/R47 → 4.98 V), AZ1117 LDO (U1) 5 V→3.3 V, three TMC2209 (U4/U10/U11) each with matched 110 mΩ sense pairs (R50/R52, R32/R15, R36/R6), 14 k/10.7 k VREF dividers on their local 5VOUT rails, shared UART on IO21/IO22 via R7, and STEP lines on IO11/IO15/IO19; two ADM3260 (U6/U7) keep the pH/EC domains galvanically separate (isolated VDD/GND only through FB1/FB6 and FB5/FB4, with 2.2 k isolated pull-ups and PDIS on IO6), the RTD sits on the non-isolated bus, and the float-switch interlocks (R46/R48, R33/R55, T8/T1) match the spec's pull directions. Reference designators and auto-generated net names are shifted relative to the spec (e.g. spec U1/U2/U3/U4/U5–U7 vs. netlist U3/U1/U6/U7/U4/U10/U11), and the TF-Luna, BME280 and BH1750 are absent as documented, but every checked net, value, rating and polarity is internally consistent, so no deviation from the intended design is supported by the files."
}

